From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: report rc when the per-play stop fails

haptics_stop_constant_effect_play() runs after every bounded FF_CONSTANT
play, but its failure log drops rc:

	rc = haptics_enable_play(chip, false);
	if (rc < 0)
		dev_err(chip->dev, "stop constant effect play failed\n");

That is the same defect 0230 fixed at the other rail sites; without rc the
one line that explains why a stop failed is useless for diagnosis. Report
it and assert the rc-bearing form in the regression test.

Fixes: 0230-input-qcom-haptics-fix-hpwr-vreg-error-log-rc.patch
---
 drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -2697,7 +2697,7 @@ static void haptics_stop_constant_effect_play(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	rc = haptics_enable_play(chip, false);
 	if (rc < 0)
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "stop constant effect play failed\n");
+		dev_err(chip->dev, "stop constant effect play failed, rc=%d\n", rc);
 
 	rc = haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg(chip, false);
 	if (rc < 0)
